  "query_preview": "..\n(Thursday through Tuesday) \nIssued at 1159 PM CDT Tue Aug 25 2026\n\nSurface high pressure and northeast to easterly winds \ntransporting drier conditions and temperatures more closer to \nseasonal average are forecast Thursday and Friday in the wake of \nthe departing boundary. This break in the current heat and heat \nstress remains forecast to be short-lived. Southerly low level \nflow returns for the weekend behind the exiting surface high \npressure. Also the parent ridge of high pressure is progged to \nexpand eastward and set up southeast of the CWA early next week. \nThus, heat and humidity returns with high temperatures back in the\nupper 90s to around 102 deg for the weekend into the first part \nof next week.",
